 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Student Data Cleaning Notebook\n",
    "This notebook loads the `students.csv` file, cleans the messy student records, and calculates summary statistics using NumPy. The workflow mirrors the logic from `task.py` so it matches the project exactly.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": "Dataset found at: students.csv\nRaw records loaded: 19\n"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "import sys\n",
    "\n",
    "candidates = [\n",
    "    Path('students.csv'),\n",
    "    Path.cwd() / 'students.csv',\n",
    "    Path.cwd() / 'week-01' / 'students.csv',\n",
    "    Path.cwd().parent / 'week-01' / 'students.csv',\n",
    "]\n",
    "\n",
    "data_path = next((p for p in candidates if p.exists()), None)\n",
    "if data_path is None:\n",
    "    raise FileNotFoundError('students.csv was not found. Keep the notebook in the same folder as the CSV file.')\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f'Dataset found at: {data_path.name}')\n",
    "\n",
    "project_dir = data_path.parent\n",
    "if str(project_dir) not in sys.path:\n",
    "    sys.path.insert(0, str(project_dir))\n",
    "\n",
    "from task import load_csv_dataset\n",
    "\n",
    "raw_records = load_csv_dataset(data_path)\n",
    "print(f'Raw records loaded: {len(raw_records)}')\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Data cleaning with functions\n",
    "The project defines reusable functions to standardize names, convert fields to numbers, fill missing values, remove duplicates, and fix invalid ages or scores. This notebook applies that same logic in a clear, step-by-step workflow.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": "Cleaned records: 15\n1. Alice Smith | age=22 | score=88.00\n2. Bob Jones | age=17 | score=76.00\n3. Carol | age=25 | score=81.00\n4. Dave Brown | age=31 | score=88.00\n5. Eve White | age=9 | score=90.00\n6. Frank | age=45 | score=95.00\n7. Grace Miller | age=25 | score=67.50\n8. Hannah | age=25 | score=72.00\n9. Ivan | age=25 | score=88.00\n10. Judy | age=28 | score=88.00\n11. Kyle | age=35 | score=84.00\n12. Liam | age=40 | score=95.00\n13. Mia | age=25 | score=88.00\n14. Nora | age=27 | score=92.00\n15. Olivia | age=30 | score=88.00\n"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "from task import clean_student_data\n",
    "\n",
    "cleaned_records = clean_student_data(raw_records)\n",
    "print(f'Cleaned records: {len(cleaned_records)}')\n",
    "for index, record in enumerate(cleaned_records, start=1):\n",
    "    print(f'{index}. {record[\'name\']} | age={float(record[\'age\']):.0f} | score={float(record[\'score\']):.2f}')\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## NumPy summary statistics\n",
    "After cleaning, the score values are converted into a NumPy array so we can compute the mean, median, standard deviation, and percentile values. These statistics help summarize the overall class performance.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": "\nSummary statistics for student scores:\nMean score: 82.37\nMedian score: 88.00\nStandard deviation: 11.32\n90th percentile: 89.20\nMinimum score: 50.00\nMaximum score: 95.00\n"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "\n",
    "scores = np.array([float(record['score']) for record in cleaned_records], dtype=float)\n",
    "stats = {\n",
    "    'mean': float(np.mean(scores)),\n",
    "    'median': float(np.median(scores)),\n",
    "    'std_dev': float(np.std(scores)),\n",
    "    'p90': float(np.percentile(scores, 90)),\n",
    "    'min': float(np.min(scores)),\n",
    "    'max': float(np.max(scores)),\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "print('\\nSummary statistics for student scores:')\n",
    "print(f\"Mean score: {stats['mean']:.2f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Median score: {stats['median']:.2f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Standard deviation: {stats['std_dev']:.2f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"90th percentile: {stats['p90']:.2f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Minimum score: {stats['min']:.2f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Maximum score: {stats['max']:.2f}\")\n"
   ]
  }
 ],
